From 2c4c11044a3a66036e6873fdbc9356c0d79bae4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:07:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] Dungeon finder: fill waiting groups with playerbots

A player who queues alone waits forever on an empty realm. Bots are now inserted into the same m_queue real players sit in, as ordinary QueuedPlayer entries, so role assignment, faction and hardcore checks, group building and the offer all run through the existing matcher - no parallel mechanism to keep in sync.

Real players keep priority: as soon as one queues, every fill bot not already part of an offer is dropped again so the human takes the slot. Bots only appear after LFT.BotFill.DelaySeconds, and only within LFT.BotFill.LevelRange of the waiting player, same faction.

Bots also honour the role they were given. Playerbot_SetForcedRole applies the tank/heal/dps strategy at the end of ResetStrategies - it has to be last, because sPlayerbotDbStore.Load runs in the middle and would otherwise overwrite it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
